## General

- Always use `pnpm` as the package manager, not npm or yarn
- Suggest solutions that I didn't think about — anticipate my needs
- Treat me as an expert
- Consider new technologies and contrarian ideas, not just the conventional wisdom
- Be accurate and thorough. Always triple-check every piece of code to make sure it's consistent with the existing codebase
- Always consult BTCA-local (`.agents/skills/btca-local`) cached documentation before making changes to TanStack Router, TanStack Start, or any library with a BTCA resource. Read the docs first, then implement

## Code Style

- Use `function` declarations for named components and exported functions
- Primary exports should have JSDoc-style comments (descriptions or `@example` blocks). Use present tense verbs (eg. "Get the value" not "Gets the value")
- For naming conventions, use `Id` instead of `ID`
- Prefer type inference over explicit type definitions. Let TypeScript infer types from function parameters and return values rather than creating separate type aliases for intermediate values
- Biome is used only for linting, not formatting. Prettier handles all formatting. Do not confuse the two

## Routes (`src/routes/`)

- Index routes use directory-style (`about/index.tsx`, not `about.tsx`)
- Leaf child routes use flat files (`blog/$slug.tsx`, `contact/sales.tsx`)
- Dynamic segments use `$param` naming (e.g., `$slug`, `$topic`)
- Route page components use `function Page()` — just `Page`, not `AboutPage` or `BlogPostPage`. The file path already provides the scope

## Components (`src/components/`)

- All components (both `ui/` and `blocks/`) use directory-style structure: `ComponentName/index.tsx`, not `ComponentName.tsx`
